  "reason": "The current best (config_008, 0.725 acc) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. The RNA encoder is the most impactful design choice (scvi_n200 ≈ 0.72 vs scgpt ≈ 0.51), but pca_n2000 has never been tested in any multimodal setting. Config_034 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) isolates the RNA encoder variable while holding all other hyperparameters at their empirically best values, directly testing whether a simpler linear PCA representation could match or exceed the generative scvi model. This is the highest-uncertainty, highest-value experiment: if pca_n2000 is competitive, it opens a new optimization axis for the remaining 3 experiments; if not, it confirms scvi_n200 is optimal and we can focus remaining budget on fine-grained refinements around the current best."
}

